That's a good point, Marc.  I suppose model selection is made easier with the multi-species construction.  But model selection won't tell you which species are strongly associated with a given site covariate, only whether all species are or are not equal in their association.  And formal pairwise tests would require some multiple comparison correction.  Depending on the number of species, the interpretation of output can become a bit muddled and overwhelming.

