I haven't had the problem myself, but I saw that at least one person determined the problem <http://r.789695.n4.nabble.com/unable-to-move-temporary-installation-td4521714.html> was caused by another program locking the temporary files. In his case it was the antivirus software.  Temporarily disabling the software fixed the problem. Another person had the same problem <http://r.789695.n4.nabble.com/Windows-7-update-packages-problem-quot-unable-to-move-temporary-installation-quot-td3456744.html>, specifically after upgrading to Windows 7, with the same solution.

